**Title:** Add loading states to async operations without them

**Description:**
Improve user experience by adding loading indicators to async operations (API calls, data fetching) that currently don't show loading states.

**Specific tasks:**
1. Find components or hooks that make async calls without loading states
2. Add loading state management (useState for loading boolean)
3. Display appropriate loading indicators during async operations
4. Ensure loading state is properly reset after completion

**Example:**
```tsx
// Before - No loading state
const UserProfile = ({ userId }) => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchUser(userId).then(setUser);
  }, [userId]);

  return <div>{user ? <h1>{user.name}</h1> : null}</div>;
};

// After - With loading state
const UserProfile = ({ userId }) => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    setLoading(true);
    fetchUser(userId)
      .then(setUser)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, [userId]);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading user...</div>;

  return <div>{user ? <h1>{user.name}</h1> : <div>User not found</div>}</div>;
};
```

**Common patterns to look for:**
- `useEffect` with async calls
- Custom hooks making API requests
- Button click handlers with async operations
- Form submissions

**Loading indicators can be:**
- Simple text ("Loading...")
- Spinner components
- Skeleton loaders
- Disabled buttons during submission

**Acceptance criteria:**
- [ ] Add loading states to at least 3-5 async operations
- [ ] Loading indicators are user-friendly
- [ ] Loading state is properly managed (set to true before, false after)
- [ ] No broken functionality
- [ ] Better user experience during waits

**Suggested files to check:**
- `src/hooks/` (custom hooks with API calls)
- `src/components/` (components with useEffect)
- Look for `fetch`, `axios`, or async functions

